## 14. Fold Expressions (C++17)

**Fold expressions** collapse (reduce) a parameter pack using a binary operator, without needing manual recursion.

### Syntax Forms

| Form | Expansion |
|---|---|
| Unary right fold `(pack op ...)` | `E1 op (E2 op (... op EN))` |
| Unary left fold `(... op pack)` | `((E1 op E2) op ...) op EN` |
| Binary right fold `(pack op ... op init)` | `E1 op (E2 op (... op (EN op init)))` |
| Binary left fold `(init op ... op pack)` | `(((init op E1) op E2) op ...) op EN` |

### Examples

```cpp
template <typename... Args>
auto sum(Args... args) {
    return (args + ...);   // unary right fold: arg1 + (arg2 + (arg3 + ...))
}

sum(1, 2, 3, 4);   // 10

template <typename... Args>
bool allTrue(Args... args) {
    return (args && ...);  // unary right fold with &&
}

allTrue(true, true, true);   // true
allTrue(true, false, true);  // false
```

### Fold with an Initial Value (binary fold)

```cpp
template <typename... Args>
auto sumWithInit(Args... args) {
    return (args + ... + 100);   // binary right fold, starts folding with 100 added at the end
}

sumWithInit(1, 2, 3);   // 1 + (2 + (3 + 100)) = 106
```

### Practical Example: Printing a Variadic Pack (Replaces Recursive Expansion)

```cpp
template <typename... Args>
void printAll(Args&&... args) {
    ((std::cout << args << " "), ...);   // unary right fold over the comma operator
    std::cout << "\n";
}

printAll(1, 2.5, "hello", 'c');   // 1 2.5 hello c
```

### Practical Example: Checking All Types Satisfy a Trait

```cpp
template <typename... Ts>
constexpr bool allIntegral = (std::is_integral_v<Ts> && ...);

static_assert(allIntegral<int, long, short>);
static_assert(!allIntegral<int, double>);
```

