## 15. if constexpr

**`if constexpr`** (C++17) evaluates a condition at **compile time** and only compiles the taken branch — the discarded branch isn't even instantiated (though it must still be syntactically valid). This eliminates a huge amount of SFINAE boilerplate for conditional logic inside templates.

```cpp
template <typename T>
auto getValue(T t) {
    if constexpr (std::is_pointer_v<T>) {
        return *t;              // only compiled if T is a pointer type
    } else {
        return t;                // only compiled if T is NOT a pointer type
    }
}

int main() {
    int x = 5;
    getValue(x);      // T = int, else-branch compiled, returns 5
    getValue(&x);      // T = int*, if-branch compiled, returns 5 (dereferenced)
}
```

### Why This Matters: the Discarded Branch Isn't Instantiated

```cpp
template <typename T>
void printSize(T val) {
    if constexpr (std::is_array_v<T>) {
        std::cout << "Array size: " << std::extent_v<T> << "\n";
    } else {
        std::cout << "Not an array, value: " << val << "\n";
        // val.someArrayOnlyMethod() would be a HARD ERROR with a regular `if`
        // even for non-array T, because both branches get compiled with `if`.
        // With `if constexpr`, the false branch is discarded entirely for non-array T.
    }
}
```

### Recursive Variadic Processing Without Recursion Depth Tricks

```cpp
template <typename T, typename... Rest>
void printAll(T first, Rest... rest) {
    std::cout << first << " ";
    if constexpr (sizeof...(rest) > 0) {   // compile-time check avoids infinite recursion
        printAll(rest...);                  // this call only compiled when there IS a rest
    }
}

printAll(1, 2, 3);   // 1 2 3
```

### Constexpr-if vs. Regular if

| | Regular `if` | `if constexpr` |
|---|---|---|
| Condition evaluated | Runtime | Compile time |
| Both branches compiled | Yes (must both be valid) | No (discarded branch is not instantiated) |
| Works outside templates | Yes | Yes, but pointless (condition must be a constant expression) |

